<div class="project-card">

<div class="project-header">
<div>
<h3>ShelfLife</h3>
<p>Food Tracking and Object Recognition Mobile App</p>
</div>

<span class="project-type">MOBILE / AI</span>
</div>

<div class="technology-list">
Java • Android • Firebase • SQLite • JSON • Computer Vision • AI
</div>

<ul>
<li>I started ShelfLife because food can easily disappear into the back of a refrigerator or cabinet until somebody forgets it is there. The app gives users a way to keep track of what they have and what might need to be used soon.</li>
<li>For image recognition, I connected a YOLO computer-vision model that can identify food from a picture. GPT is used in areas where generated information fits the feature.</li>
<li>Expiration information can be saved with an item, making it easier to see which food has been around the longest.</li>
<li>Early versions relied heavily on JSON files. That became awkward as the amount of information grew, so I transferred the data into SQLite and made it searchable directly on the device.</li>
<li>Firebase takes care of authentication. Other versions of the project have included barcode scanning, local device storage, and AI-generated recipe ideas.</li>
<li>As ShelfLife grew, some files became much larger than they needed to be. I broke those sections into smaller classes and components so changing one feature wouldn't mean digging through one enormous file.</li>
</ul>

