<div class="project-card">

<div class="project-header">
<div>
<h3>GiggleBot</h3>
<p>Educational AI Web Application</p>
</div>

<span class="project-type">FULL-STACK / AI</span>
</div>

<div class="technology-list">
JavaScript • Node.js • Express.js • EJS • MongoDB • OpenAI API • Render
</div>

<ul>
<li>GiggleBot began as an experiment with using AI for children's stories, conversation, and learning activities. I wanted the application to have more going on than simply putting a new interface around a chatbot.</li>
<li>Messages are sent to my server before reaching the OpenAI API, keeping that part of the application out of the browser.</li>
<li>MongoDB holds conversation information, while sessions preserve the information the application needs as somebody moves between pages.</li>
<li>I intentionally kept the screens uncomplicated. With children as the intended users, filling every page with buttons and settings didn't make much sense.</li>
<li>Different features have their own backend routes rather than everything running through one route. The project is hosted on Render, but I still use it to experiment and make changes.</li>
</ul>

