<div class="technology-list">
React Native • Expo • TypeScript • Supabase
</div>

<ul>
<li>Mission Trail grew out of an idea for a mobile app centered on outdoor activities and location-based missions. Over time, I added progression and ways for users to interact with one another.</li>
<li>My early screens got too large. Features that had nothing to do with each other were living in the same files, which made even small changes irritating. I've gradually separated those sections into smaller components.</li>
<li>Registration and onboarding went through several versions. Testing the app on an actual phone made it obvious that some steps I originally thought were necessary were really just getting in the way.</li>
<li>I made a similar change with database and authentication code. Logic that had been mixed directly into the screens has been moved away from the interface when it doesn't need to be there.</li>
<li>More of my recent work has been on things that become noticeable when using the app rather than just reading its code: navigation, different screen sizes, animation, layout, and how one screen moves into another.</li>
<li>The original version came from coursework. I kept developing it after the class finished because I wanted to find out how far I could take the idea.</li>
</ul>

